# AWS Cloud Operations Assignment Summary

This assignment covers 6 lab questions spanning multiple AWS modules, demonstrating core cloud operations skills.

---

## Lab 1 — Module 2: Create a Static Website on S3

**Objective:** Host a static website using Amazon S3.

**Steps:** SSH into an EC2 instance, create an S3 bucket, configure it for public static website hosting, upload website files, create a shell script to automate updates, and optimize using `sync` instead of `cp`.

**Key CLI Commands:**

| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `sudo chmod 600 labsuser.pem` | Set secure permissions on the PEM key |
| `ssh -i labsuser.pem ec2-user@<IP>` | SSH into EC2 instance |
| `aws configure` | Configure AWS CLI credentials and region |
| `aws s3 ls` | List S3 buckets |
| `aws s3api create-bucket --bucket <name> --region eu-west-2 --create-bucket-configuration LocationConstraint=eu-west-2` | Create S3 bucket in a specific region |
| `tar xvzf static-website.tar.gz` | Extract the website archive |
| `sudo rm -rf static-website.tar.gz` | Remove the archive after extraction |
| `aws s3api put-bucket-ownership-controls --bucket <name> --ownership-controls "Rules=[{ObjectOwnership=BucketOwnerPreferred}]"` | Set bucket ownership controls |
| `aws s3api put-public-access-block --bucket <name> --public-access-block-configuration "BlockPublicAcls=false,IgnorePublicAcls=false,BlockPublicPolicy=false,RestrictPublicBuckets=false"` | Disable public access block |
| `aws s3 website s3://<bucket>/ --index-document index.html` | Configure bucket for static website hosting |
| `aws s3 cp . s3://<bucket>/ --recursive --acl public-read` | Upload all files to S3 with public read ACL |
| `aws s3 ls <bucket>` | Verify bucket contents |
| `aws s3 sync ~/sysops-activity-files/ s3://<bucket>/ --acl public-read` | Sync local files to S3 (more efficient than cp) |

