## Lab 3 — Module 7: Troubleshoot VPC

**Objective:** Fix VPC connectivity issues and analyze VPC Flow Logs.

**Steps:** Set up Flow Logs to S3, investigate SSH timeout by checking security groups, route tables, and Network ACLs, then add a missing internet gateway route and remove a blocking ACL rule.

**Root Causes Found:**
- Missing route to Internet Gateway in route table
- Network ACL explicitly denying port 22 (SSH)

**Key CLI Commands:**

| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `aws s3api create-bucket --bucket <name> --region us-east-1` | Create bucket for flow logs |
| `aws ec2 describe-vpcs --query 'Vpcs[*].[VpcId,Tags[?Key==Name].Value,CidrBlock]' --filters 'Name=tag:Name,Values=VPC1'` | Get VPC ID for VPC1 |
| `aws ec2 create-flow-logs --resource-type VPC --resource-ids <vpc-id> --traffic-type ALL --log-destination-type s3 --log-destination arn:aws:s3:::<bucket>` | Enable VPC Flow Logs to S3 |
| `aws ec2 describe-flow-logs` | Verify flow log creation |
| `aws ec2 describe-instances --filter "Name=ip-address,Values=<IP>" --query 'Reservations[*].Instances[*].[State,PrivateIpAddress,InstanceId,SecurityGroups,SubnetId,KeyName]'` | Get web server instance details |
| `sudo ssh -i labsuser.pem ec2-user@<IP> -o ConnectTimeout=10` | Attempt SSH (reveals timeout) |
| `aws ec2 describe-security-groups` | Check security group rules |
| `aws ec2 describe-route-tables` | Get route table ID |
| `aws ec2 describe-internet-gateways` | Get internet gateway ID |
| `aws ec2 create-route --route-table-id <rtb-id> --destination-cidr-block 0.0.0.0/0 --gateway-id <igw-id>` | Add route to internet gateway |
| `aws ec2 describe-network-acls --filter "Name=association.subnet-id,Values=<subnet-id>" --query 'NetworkAcls[*].[NetworkAclId,Entries]'` | Check Network ACL rules |
| `aws ec2 delete-network-acl-entry --network-acl-id <acl-id> --rule-number 40 --ingress` | Remove blocking ACL rule for port 22 |
| `mkdir flowlogs && cd flowlogs` | Create directory for flow log download |
| `aws s3 cp s3://<bucket>/ . --recursive` | Download flow logs from S3 |
| `gunzip *.gz` | Extract compressed log files |
| `grep -rn REJECT` | Find all rejected traffic in logs |
| `grep -rn REJECT . \| wc -l` | Count total rejected entries |
| `grep -rn ' 22 ' . \| grep REJECT` | Filter rejections on port 22 |

