## Lab 5 — Module 9: Working with AWS CloudTrail

**Objective:** Investigate a security breach using CloudTrail logs, Athena queries, and OS-level forensics.

**Security Incident:** A "chaos" user hacked the web server — changed the homepage image, added an SSH inbound rule open to 0.0.0.0/0, created an OS user, and modified sshd_config.

**Key CLI Commands:**

| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `mkdir ctraillogs && cd ctraillogs` | Create directory for CloudTrail logs |
| `aws s3 ls` | List buckets to find the monitoring bucket |
| `aws s3 cp s3://<monitoring-bucket>/ . --recursive` | Download all CloudTrail logs |
| `gunzip *.gz` | Decompress log files |
| `cat <filename.json> \| python -m json.tool` | Pretty-print JSON log for readability |
| `ip=<WebServerIP>` | Set shell variable for web server IP |
| `for i in $(ls); do echo $i && cat $i \| python -m json.tool \| grep sourceIPAddress; done` | Iterate logs and filter by source IP |
| `for i in $(ls); do echo $i && cat $i \| python -m json.tool \| grep eventName; done` | Iterate logs and filter by event name |
| `aws cloudtrail lookup-events --lookup-attributes AttributeKey=EventName,AttributeValue=ConsoleLogin` | Look up console login events |
| `aws ec2 describe-instances --filters "Name=tag:Name,Values='Cafe Web Server'" --query 'Reservations[*].Instances[*].SecurityGroups[*].[GroupId]' --region <region> --output text \| grep $sgId` | Find security group of web server |
| `aws cloudtrail lookup-events --lookup-attributes AttributeKey=ResourceType,AttributeValue=AWS::EC2::SecurityGroup --region <region> --output text \| grep $sgId` | Find events targeting the security group |
| `sudo aureport --auth` | View OS authentication/login report |
| `who` | Show currently logged-in users |
| `sudo userdel -r chaos-user` | Delete the malicious OS user |
| `sudo kill -9 <ProcNum>` | Force-kill the active chaos-user session |
| `sudo cat /etc/passwd \| grep -v nologin` | List users who can log in |
| `sudo ls -l /etc/ssh/sshd_config` | Check sshd_config modification timestamp |
| `sudo vi /etc/ssh/sshd_config` | Edit SSH config to disable password auth |
| `sudo service sshd restart` | Restart SSH service to apply changes |
| `cd /var/www/html/mompopcafe/images/ && sudo mv Coffee-and-Pastries.backup Coffee-and-Pastries.png` | Restore original website image |
| `aws iam delete-login-profile --user-name chaos-user` | Delete hacker's IAM console login |
| `grep -rn ' 22 ' . \| grep REJECT \| grep <ip-address>` | Find SSH rejection logs from specific IP |
| `aws ec2 describe-network-interfaces --filters "Name=association.public-ip,Values=<IP>" --query 'NetworkInterfaces[*].[NetworkInterfaceId,Association.PublicIp]'` | Verify ENI matches flow log entries |
| `date -d @<unix_timestamp>` | Convert Unix timestamp to readable date |

**Athena Queries Used:**
```sql
SELECT * FROM cloudtrail_logs_aman_msis_7272 LIMIT 5;

SELECT useridentity.username, eventtime, eventsource, eventname, requestparameters
FROM cloudtrail_logs_aman_msis_7272 LIMIT 30;

SELECT DISTINCT useridentity.username, eventName, eventSource
FROM cloudtrail_logs_aman_msis_7272
WHERE from_iso8601_timestamp(eventtime) > date_add('day', -1, now())
ORDER BY eventSource;
```

