## Lab 6 — Module 8: Working with S3 (IAM + SNS Notifications)

**Objective:** Demonstrate S3 access control using IAM users and configure S3 event notifications via SNS.

**Steps:** Create S3 bucket, upload images, review IAM user permissions (mediacouser), test upload/delete/get/ACL operations as that user, create an SNS topic with email subscription, configure S3 event notifications via JSON policy, trigger and verify email alerts.

**Key CLI Commands:**

| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `aws s3 mb s3://<bucket> --region us-east-1` | Create a new S3 bucket |
| `aws s3 sync ~/initial-images/ s3://<bucket>/images` | Upload images to S3 images prefix |
| `aws s3 ls s3://<bucket>/images/ --human-readable --summarize` | List bucket contents with sizes |
| `aws s3api put-object --bucket <bucket> --key images/<file> --body <local-file>` | Upload a single object to S3 |
| `aws s3api get-object --bucket <bucket> --key images/<file> <local-filename>` | Download an object from S3 |
| `aws s3api delete-object --bucket <bucket> --key images/<file>` | Delete an object from S3 |
| `aws s3api put-object-acl --bucket <bucket> --key images/<file> --acl public-read` | Attempt to set public ACL (blocked by policy) |
| `nano s3EventNotification.json` | Create S3 event notification config file |
| `aws s3api put-bucket-notification-configuration --bucket <bucket> --notification-configuration file://s3EventNotification.json` | Apply S3 event notification config |

